Task: Implement OrderStore.postgres via Skunk (Green)

Summary: Added OrderStore.postgres[F: Async: Console: Network](config): Resource[F,
OrderStore[F]], using Skunk's Session.Builder(...).pooled(max = 10) fluent API (the
deprecated Session.pooled(...) overload was avoided). create() checks out a session
from the pool per call, generates a UUID, and inserts a row via a prepared Command.
otel4s Tracer/Meter no-op instances are summoned locally since this project doesn't yet
wire Skunk's own tracing/metrics integration into purerest's tracer (out of scope for
this track — could be revisited as a purerest-observability enhancement later).

Files changed:
- modules/order-service/src/main/scala/orderservice/OrderStore.scala

Verified: OrderStorePostgresSuite green (2/2) against real Testcontainers Postgres; zero
compiler warnings (fixed two Skunk 1.0.0 deprecation warnings — Session.pooled and the
implicit Network derivation — by using the Builder API and an explicit Network[F]
context bound).
